# Rime OS — the one Secret Service provider this image ships.
#
# Installed to /usr/share/rime/secrets-provider. The ONE place the provider's
# name is written down. Read by:
#
#   Containerfile.base    the portal assertions (each session's portals.conf
#                         must pin `org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Secret=<portal>`
#                         and <portal>.portal must exist) and the build guard
#                         that refuses a second org.freedesktop.secrets provider
#   rime-secrets-start    which daemon the session starts first
#   rime-keyring-login    acts only when the provider is gnome-keyring
#
# A reader that finds no file treats it as `provider=gnome-keyring`, which is
# what every Rime release before this file shipped.
#
# Why gnome-keyring and not oo7, although Fedora 45 moved its desktops to
# oo7-daemon: Rime unlocks the keyring at login through pam_gnome_keyring and
# turns a machine's existing keyring into the login keyring with
# rime-keyring-login, which reads gnome-keyring's file format. oo7 is a beta
# with a different store and a different PAM module. Moving is a decision of
# its own, and it starts by changing this file.
#
# provider  the daemon that owns org.freedesktop.secrets: gnome-keyring | oo7
# portal    the xdg-desktop-portal backend for org.freedesktop.impl.portal.Secret
#           (the basename of its .portal file: gnome-keyring, or oo7-portal)
provider=gnome-keyring
portal=gnome-keyring
